of a fixed, random network (the reservoir) to process input data, making it particularly useful for tasks like anomaly detection.\n\nThe summaries of the most recent arXiv papers did not mention ESNs. Here is a brief synthesis based on the Wikipedia summary: ESNs use a large, randomly connected hidden layer to process time series data, with only the readout layer being trained.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1207,"prompt_eval_duration":47101000,"total_duration":2019692300}}